target: internal/record/record.go
verify: go test ./internal/record/ -count=1 -run 'TestTheDecodeErrorNamesWhatTheOperatorMustGoFix'
expect: a hidden second bad field is a second round trip
why:    restores the exact keep-first behaviour the accumulation replaced, which the paragraph above setErr argues against at length and which no test covered — no fixture had two bad rows in one run. encoding/json reports whichever bad field comes first in the WRITER's key order, and across rows the first bad row in file order, so keep-first measurably put `n` (which nothing derives from) in the message while hiding `unresolved_asks`, the one field whose misreading motivated this whole layer.
